{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChLPvB7t3DkBu5fkcAzkn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`Sum(Sum(e[i, j], (i, 0, n-1)), (j, 0, n-1)).doit()` now returns `n`, as the issue expects. One existing test, `test_Sum_doit`, now fails because of the second change below.\n\nThe issue's own example goes through `refine` on `M.T * M`. I didn't run that. I checked the sum on a plain `Identity(n)`, which is what that expression reduces to.\n\nI made two changes:\n\n- **`Identity._entry`** in `sympy/matrices/expressions/matexpr.py`: it now returns `1` or `0` only when `i` and `j` are provably equal or unequal. Otherwise it returns `KroneckerDelta(i, j)`. Before, symbolic `i` and `j` fell through to `0`, which is why the total came out as 0.\n- **`eval_sum`** in `sympy/concrete/summations.py`: the inner sum over a `KroneckerDelta` leaves `Piecewise((1, (0 <= j) & (j <= n-1)), (0, True))`, and the outer sum couldn't simplify it. I added a shortcut. If a `Piecewise`'s first condition is exactly the summation range, the sum uses its first expression.\n\nThe failing test, `test_Sum_doit` in `sympy/concrete/tests/test_sums_products.py`, asserts that `Sum(Piecewise((1, And(1 <= n, n <= N)), (0, True)), (n, 1, N)).doit()` stays unevaluated. With the shortcut it evaluates to `N`, which is mathematically correct but contradicts that assertion. I can't edit tests, so I left it failing. If you'd rather keep that test passing, the shortcut would need a different approach, and I haven't tried one.\n\nI compared `sympy/matrices` and `sympy/concrete` against a clean checkout. The only new failure is `test_Sum_doit`. The other failures were already there."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":717,"cache_read_input_tokens":28479,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":717},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e9524ce5-cd11-4459-9411-24227431f8cc","uuid":"1939fe7d-c715-45ea-b973-69f8087b2e75","timestamp":"2026-11-23T19:16:23.422Z","request_id":"req_011ChLPvAyCet9iKNLEfBxgH"}
